  [few-pictures] @1440px  Only 0 picture(s) on the page (0 photographs, footage or raster images, 0 interface fragments). Drawings in SVG do not count.
      → Find real pictures of the subject's world with scripts/assets.mjs (photographs, archival images, maps, engravings, footage), download them to assets/ and give them room: a hero picture, one per section that has a subject, a full-width band. At least four, usually six to twelve.
  [headline-lines] @768px  1 headline(s) wrap past two lines at 768px: ""EVERY PICTURE TELLS A STORY. Let us help you wr" → 4 lines (11 words, 60px)
      → Cut words first (a headline is a title, not a sentence). Then give it a wider measure. Lower the size only as a last resort and never below the scale you chose. A real statement paragraph belongs in a <p> or <blockquote> at 32px or less.
  [off-centre] @768px  The page sits off-centre: its content comes to 80px from the left edge but only to 0px from the right, at 768px.
      → Give the page one pair of equal margins. Check the wrapper for a max-width without margin-inline: auto, a grid with an empty last column, or padding on one side only. If one side is meant to hold air, it must still be closed by something that reaches the margin (a picture, the navigation's last item, a figure).
